      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I am Dr. Smith. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, hi Dr. Smith. What brings me in... I guess it's that I feel like I'm always moving from one thing to the next, you know? Like I just can't idle. It's funny, my wife says I'm like that old lawnmower we used to have, the one that wouldn't shut off unless you pulled the spark plug wire. We had this huge yard back in Ohio, took me three hours to mow it every Saturday. Anyway, the new work setup has made it a lot harder to hide that I can't sit still. They put us all in these open-plan pods now, which is just ridiculous if you ask me. The lighting in there gives me a headache too, it's that weird blue fluorescent kind. But yeah, the constant moving around is why I'm here.",
