    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back at your life, have you always felt this way, even when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, yeah, definitely. I mean, looking back, this was around long before the new job setup. Even in grade school, my teachers were always writing on my report cards that I was bright but careless, you know? They said I talked out of turn and always had to be reminded to stay with my work. It's funny thinking about grade school, I went to this little brick schoolhouse, Lincoln Elementary. They tore it down a few years ago to build a strip mall. Such a shame, really. I remember Mrs. Gable, my third-grade teacher, she had this massive collection of porcelain frogs on her desk. Hundreds of them. I knocked one over once when I was supposed to be in my seat... broke its little leg off. I tried to glue it back on with that white paste we used to use, but it never looked right again. But anyway, yeah, I've always been like this.",
