    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Beyond the constant need to move, do you often find that you have trouble focusing on tasks or that you frequently make careless mistakes?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S001",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, the careless mistakes... that happens a lot, actually. Like at work, I do customer service, right? And I’ll think I’ve completely finished a customer ticket, everything's good to go. But then later I’ll notice I typed the wrong account number, or I just totally skipped one of the required boxes. Or I'll miss one little instruction that makes the whole thing come back to me. \n\nSpeaking of things coming back, the new software system they gave us is just a nightmare for that. They rolled it out right around Halloween. I remember because my neighbor had this giant inflatable spider on his roof, and the wind kept blowing its legs over onto my side of the property line and into my gutters. I had to get the ladder out twice to push it away, and my gutters really needed cleaning anyway... they get completely choked up with oak leaves this time of year. We have this massive oak tree in the front yard, probably a hundred years old. Drops leaves from October straight through Thanksgiving. But anyway, yeah, the new software has all these tiny little fields on the screen, so it's really easy for me to miss one little box, and then the ticket just bounces right back to my queue.",
