    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "In your daily life as an adult, do you frequently find yourself acting impulsively, such as blurting out answers, interrupting others, or having difficulty waiting your turn?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S018",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I guess... I mean, I really don't mean to be rude about it, but at work, if I hear my coworkers trying to work through a customer problem, I’ll just jump right in with an answer before they’ve even finished explaining it. Or before anyone even asked me for help, honestly. It just sort of comes out. \n\nSpeaking of my coworkers, the guy in the pod next to me, Gary, he just got this new car. It's one of those electric ones, completely silent. I almost walked right into it in the parking lot on Tuesday. Scared the living daylights out of me. I don't trust a car you can't hear running. My first car was a '78 Chevy Nova, and believe me, you could hear that thing coming from three blocks away. Needed a new muffler every other year, it felt like. I used to take it down to this guy Sal on 4th Street, he had a shop behind the old diner. Best mechanic I ever knew, though his waiting room always smelled like burnt coffee. \n\nBut anyway, what were we... oh, right, interrupting. Yeah, I definitely do that a lot with the other reps.",
